      "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y=\\frac{1}{4}f(x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and compress it by factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nThe resulting graph is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227189/assets/e7f418df59b24e1410b172f362c087241b85c0fa9861231ec352f80cbc0668ff.png)",
